{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35269","model_call":22,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"marshall plan\" (+ \"continued prosperity\" \"prosperity of the united states\" \"economic health\") (+ exports markets trade))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"marshall plan\" (+ \"continued prosperity\" \"prosperity of the united states\" \"economic health\") (+ exports markets trade))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_593142720#6_869534727","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1398","rank":1,"snippet":"Articles by Kennan: Links: Dean Acheson Encyclopedias: \" , \"segment\": \"Kennan called for a “long-term, patient but firm and vigilant containment of Russian expansive tendencies.” Secretary of State Marshall appointed Kennan to head a planning group to assess whether European nations could resist Soviet expansion. Kennan quickly reported that the war had left Europe in terrible economic shape. He reported on the grim realities in Europe: • Many survivors of the war were homeless, hungry, and unemployed. • Inflation robbed the wages of those who were employed. • Factories, railroads, bridges, electric power plants, and water systems were damaged or destroyed. • Farmers suffered from drought and when they brought their products to market, city dwellers could not afford them. • <cover>Trade and the flow of capital needed to finance reconstruction were interrupted. Kennan recommended that the United States help rebuild “the economic health and vigor of European society.”\" , \"start_char\": 3011.000000 , \"title\": \"Constitutional Rights Foundation\" , \"url\": \"http://www.crf-usa.org/bill-of-rights-in-action/bria-20-3-a-the-marshall-plan-</cover>for-rebuilding-western-europe.html\" }"},"time":1055},"model_calls":22,"document_judgments":18,"relevance_3":6,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
