{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35269","model_call":41,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":20809,"output_tokens":232,"total_tokens":21041,"cached_tokens":17152,"reasoning_tokens":45},"output_characters":879,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_244546227#10_450582969","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a dedicated Marshall Plan article and directly states that the plan promoted open markets and free trade in Europe, allowing American exporters to enter European markets more easily than before World War II. That directly supports how American leaders expected the plan to help American businesses, though it overlaps with the prior segment from the same source.","learned":"The Marshall Plan was expected to help U.S. businesses by liberalizing European economies, encouraging free trade, and making European markets more accessible to American exporters."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1404","reason":"The current query is yielding direct evidence about American exporters, markets, and free trade benefits from the Marshall Plan; continue while it remains productive."}}}
